@1 = ~Oh, hello. A lovelier group of adventurers I haven't seen in a while, petal. Tis dangerous to venture into the wilderness beyond safety of Beregost. Come to my hideout, my love. The entrance is just in the back of the house.~
@2 = ~Now we can talk, petal. You look weary after your travels. Fancy some tea?~
@3 = ~What would you like to know, petal?~
@4 = ~Who are you and why do you live in a flooded house?~
@5 = ~What is that foul smell in the air?~
@6 = ~That locked altar…~
@7 = ~I think we'll be leaving. Thank you… for everything. I guess.~
@8 = ~Oh dear, my apologies for skipping introductions. You can call me Ethel. Or Auntie Ethel as locals tend to call me. Some also call me a witch or a hag, and in certain way… they are correct. As for your second question, I do not live here. This musty hole is but a temporary lair.~
@9 = ~Mustn't I remind you that you are my quest, petal. It'd be considerate of you to show me respect. If we were back at my teahouse at Sunlit Wetlands, I'd make you cuppa and tell you to put your feet up. Alas, here I can only encourage you to follow the rules of common decency and play according to my rules.~
@10 = ~Let me stop your train of thoughts right there, petal. This is MY hideout, and therefore I do not condone interest with me personal belongings. You do not see me rummaging through your backpack now, do you?~
@11 = ~I am simply curious.~
@12 = ~It's almost as if you've got something to hide.~
@13 = ~Step aside, old hag or I will make you!~
@14 = ~My apologies, Ethel. I didn't mean to be nosy.~
@15 = ~Curiosity kills naughty cats, petal. I guarantee you that my belongings are nothing special. They are simply… sentimental. Valuable for me. Which is why I will keep it my business, love. That way we can go separate ways in peace.~
@16 = ~I like you, petal. Which is why I intend to keep things civil. You are welcome to stay and have a cuppa with me, or rest before you resume your travels or… you and I will find ourselves at an impasse. A remarkably inescapable impasse. How's it gonna be, petal?~
@17 = ~Oh, you want to play the hero so badly? Fine. Let's make this interesting. You asked for it, petal.~
@18 = ~Brrr, this woman sends a shiver down my spine. I know she is nice and all but... something feels… off.~
@19 = ~Boo's fur stands on end because of that woman. And it do so only when he feels something is wrong. I'd tread carefully.~
@20 = ~As much as I enjoy our little pop in to see that elderly… lady, I'd be more than joyful if we pop out. At once.~
@21 = ~This may sound unusual from my mouth but... the aura around this witch fills me with uncommon feeling of dread. Whatever you want to say to her, do so with caution. We do not know what she is capable of.~
@22 = ~I see her rummaging through our intestines if we do not leave instantly. Do I need to remind you, oh leader, to not make hasty decisions that bring us closer to our impending doom?~
@23 = ~It's all right, petal. Let us forget about this little inconvenience and move on with our respective lives.~
@24 = ~What is it, petal?~
@30 = ~Auntie Ethel~
@31 = ~Auntie Ethel~
@32 = ~The Key to Ethel's altar~
@33 = ~A key with an unsettlingly ornate design. It appears to open the locked altar in Auntie Ethel's hideout.~

@34 = ~Ethel's Skull~
@35 = ~This mysterious helmet seems to be carved from human skull. The scalp is adorned with various sophisticated symbols of unknown meanings. Dark magic is clearly swimming through this piece of armor albeit its effects don't appear to be harmful.

Equipped abilities:
- +50 magic protection
- +1 to intelligence~
